{#
The warning on a draft whose send finally failed (#125) — on its row in the
Drafts list, and on the Drafts entry in the sidebar while any draft has one.

One icon in both places, defined once, so the sidebar's mark is plainly the
same thing as the row's and the reader knows what to look for when they open
Drafts. Red, because it is the one state here that means "this did not happen
and you need to know": the toast that said so is gone by the time a scheduled
send's failure is noticed.

The sidebar's is rendered at every count and hidden at zero, the idiom every
patched marker follows (see _new_dot.html.twig): ui--sidebar finds it by
`data-count-key` after a counts refresh, and an element never rendered cannot
be found.

`hidden` goes on a wrapper, never on the <i>: Font Awesome's .fa-solid sets
`display` and lands after Tailwind's utilities, so a `hidden` on the icon is
overridden and the mark shows at zero — which is how it first shipped, on every
install, with no draft marked at all. _thread_row.html.twig wraps its icons for
the same reason.
#}
{% macro row(failure) %}
    {% set reason = ('thread_row.send_failed.' ~ failure.value)|trans %}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation shrink-0 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400"
       role="img"
       data-unsent-draft
       title="{{ reason }}"
       aria-label="{{ reason }}"></i>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro sidebar(count) %}
    {# No display utility beside `hidden`: one of those would be a second
       `display` competing with it, and it lost to `inline-flex` here once. #}
    <span class="text-xs{{ count > 0 ? '' : ' hidden' }}"
          role="img"
          data-unsent-mark
          data-count-key="unsent:role:drafts"
          title="{{ 'sidebar.badge.unsent'|trans }}"
          aria-label="{{ 'sidebar.badge.unsent'|trans }}">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-red-600 dark:text-red-400" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </span>
{% endmacro %}
